# What's Being Built

A simple personal map app for tracking building and construction projects in St. Petersburg, FL.

## How to run locally

Use VS Code Live Server.

Right-click `index.html` and choose:

Open with Live Server

To test from a phone on the same Wi-Fi network, serve the folder on all local interfaces:

```powershell
.\scripts\serve-local.ps1 -HostName 0.0.0.0 -Port 5173
```

This uses Node, which is already needed by the planned Vite/React stack. Then open `http://YOUR_PC_IP:5173` on the phone. Use `ipconfig` to find the PC's Wi-Fi IPv4 address. If Windows asks about firewall access, allow private-network access for local testing.

Phone location and heading may require HTTPS in some browsers. For full mobile testing, use a free HTTPS deploy or a trusted local HTTPS tunnel.

## How data works

The map loads project markers from `projects.json`.

To add a new project, add a new object to `projects.json`.

`private_database.json` is for private research notes and extra project details.

## Map provider boundary

The app currently uses MapLibre, but feature code should go through the `mapView` provider boundary in `index.html`. That keeps project data, markers, user location, imagery switching, and 3D controls easier to move later if the app upgrades to a higher-quality 3D map provider.
